# What must never reach a build context.
#
# Two of these are not tidiness. `.env` holds every credential this platform
# has, and an image is copied to a registry and pulled by anybody with access
# to it. `vendor` and `node_modules` are a developer's machine: copying them in
# would put dev dependencies — Faker, PHPUnit, Pail — into an image that faces
# the internet, on top of the ones the Dockerfile deliberately left out.

**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

**/vendor
**/node_modules

# Build output. The images build their own; a stale local copy shipping
# instead is a deploy of whatever was last built on somebody's laptop.
**/dist
# Except the design tokens, which are not build output in that sense: they are
# committed, CI fails if they drift from tokens.json, and both web apps import
# them straight from this folder. No image regenerates them, so without them
# the console and the public site have no stylesheet to build.
!packages/tokens/dist
**/.angular
apps/api/bootstrap/cache/*.php
apps/api/public/build

# Anything a developer's machine wrote that a server has no use for.
**/storage/logs/*
**/storage/framework/cache/*
**/storage/framework/sessions/*
**/storage/framework/views/*
**/.phpunit.cache
**/coverage

# The phone app's platform folders: built by Capacitor, not by a server.
apps/mobile/android
apps/mobile/ios

.git
.github
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
